Linux kernel
============

The Linux kernel is the core of any Linux operating system. It manages hardware,
system resources, and provides the fundamental services for all other software.

A733 BSP fork maintenance
------------------------

The honsunrise/a733-bsp-v7.2 branch merges official stable v7.2.10
(7b20d05fd38de8e0be168956f6fd241d750c7d69) into the existing Radxa BSP
forward port. It retains the bsp/ providers and the Cubie A7A/A7S/A7Z DTBs;
the validated runtime target is the A7A with its UFS combo module.

Five separately committed fixes are imported from the validated Nix source:
HDMI detection trace gating, the MMC UHS-II host callback guard, A733
GMAC210 support in dwmac-sun55i, the A7A GMAC resource/PHY setup (including
tx-queue-0 and rx-queue-0 IRQ names), and the UFS level-high IRQ baseline.
None is superseded by v7.2.10. The GMAC driver is based on Jerome Brunet's
2026-07-31 RFC, with the locally validated reset, DMA and PHY clock fixes.
The UFS interrupt trigger is a preserved bring-up setting, not a verified
hardware requirement; the vendor DT describes an edge-rising interrupt.
No experimental UFS IRQ/error-handler changes are carried.

The 7.2 API adaptations also migrate sunxi DRM atomic transactions to
drm_atomic_commit and replace removed strncpy calls in the enabled pinctrl,
RTC, NSI, SID, sysinfo and power-key drivers. Bounded input copies retain
termination and parser limits; unsupported drivers are not enabled or used
as substitutes for these fixes. The Iris IRQ/runtime-PM corrections preserve
the complete synchronization and reference-counting fix as one unit.

The configuration interface remains:

  make ARCH=arm64 BSP_TOP=bsp/ LICHEE_KERN_DIR=./ \
       KBUILD_DEFCONFIG=bsp.config defconfig radxa.config radxa_custom.config

Pass the usual CROSS_COMPILE and O= settings for the toolchain/build tree.
The cpufreq provider is pinned to its existing cpufreq-linux-7.1 directory
instead of constructing a nonexistent directory from VERSION.PATCHLEVEL.
Its previously unsupported drivers remain disabled; no new hardware is
enabled by this stable update. Mainline stmmac is explicit in the final
fragment, replacing the obsolete vendor-GMAC expectation.

Makefile reports 7.2.10 with empty EXTRAVERSION. The final fragment clears
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION and disables CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO; the default
exported empty LOCALVERSION prevents an implicit Git '+' suffix. Explicit
caller suffixes remain supported. Nix retains responsibility for its
embedded initramfs, root preparation, CPU_IDLE/PREEMPT/RCU settings and
the measured boot command line, including irqpoll.

The 7.1.3 runtime baseline was validated before this migration. Validate each
7.2.10 update with the consuming Nix configuration, including the generated
config, kernel/modules and Cubie DTBs. A successful build is not a substitute
for physical A7A UFS/Ethernet and boot validation before deployment.

Quick Start
-----------

* Report a bug: See Documentation/admin-guide/reporting-issues.rst
* Get the latest kernel: https://kernel.org
* Build the kernel: See Documentation/admin-guide/quickly-build-trimmed-linux.rst
* Join the community: https://lore.kernel.org/

Essential Documentation
-----------------------

All users should be familiar with:

* Building requirements: Documentation/process/changes.rst
* Code of Conduct: Documentation/process/code-of-conduct.rst
* License: See COPYING

Documentation can be built with make htmldocs or viewed online at:
https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/


Who Are You?
============

Find your role below:

* New Kernel Developer - Getting started with kernel development
* Academic Researcher - Studying kernel internals and architecture
* Security Expert - Hardening and vulnerability analysis
* Backport/Maintenance Engineer - Maintaining stable kernels
* System Administrator - Configuring and troubleshooting
* Maintainer - Leading subsystems and reviewing patches
* Hardware Vendor - Writing drivers for new hardware
* Distribution Maintainer - Packaging kernels for distros
* AI Coding Assistant - LLMs and AI-powered development tools


